  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to Colorado totaled $302M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 97.9% year over year. Award activity shows 1,062 awards with an average award size of $285K. Yearly totals before FY2027 show a sustained multi-year scale: FY22 was $14.3B, FY23 was $15.4B, FY24 was $15.6B, FY25 was $16.5B, and FY26 was $14.5B. The current-year total is partial because fiscal year to date figures are reported. The top buying agencies in FY2027 to date are the Department of Homeland Security with $89.1M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $73.1M, and the Department of the Interior with $40.8M. The leading vendors in FY2027 to date include ARDENT GROUP, LLC at $44.8M, THE GEO GROUP, INC. at $39.9M, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP at $35M. Top industries by NAICS include Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds at $44.8M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $41.1M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did federal contracting in Colorado change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 97.9% year over year in FY2027 to date. Total federal contract obligations for Colorado are $302M in FY2027 to date, down from prior full-year totals that ranged from $14.3B to $16.5B in FY22 through FY26. Award-level activity shows 1,062 awards, with an average award size of $285K, and the FY2027 figure is a fiscal year to date partial total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors are the top buyers and suppliers in Colorado?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, and Department of the Interior are the top three buying agencies in FY2027 to date with $89.1M, $73.1M, and $40.8M respectively. ARDENT GROUP, LLC, THE GEO GROUP, INC., and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP are the top three vendors in FY2027 to date with $44.8M, $39.9M, and $35M respectively. Industry concentration in FY2027 to date is led by Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds at $44.8M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $41.1M."
      }
