      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Colorado?",
      "a": "Colorado received $302M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state has 1,062 awards so far with an average award size of $285K, and obligations fell 97.9% year over year. FY22 through FY26 full-year obligations were $14.3B, $15.4B, $15.6B, $16.5B, and $14.5B respectively."
